ROLE: systems_reviewer  VOTE: yellow
EXISTING_IMPLEMENTATIONS: [{system: "SGLang / RadixAttention", url: "https://arxiv.org/html/2312.07104v1", overlap: "High: Section 5.2 says cache-aware scheduling for continuous batching sorts waiting requests by matched prefix length instead of FCFS to improve cache hit rate; this directly overlaps PFA admission."}, {system: "vLLM Automatic Prefix Caching", url: "https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/design/prefix_caching/", overlap: "Medium: shipping block-hash APC with LRU eviction and full-block reuse; evidence found for cache mechanism, not for bounded fairness-aware admission."}, {system: "TensorRT-LLM KV cache reuse", url: "https://nvidia.github.io/TensorRT-LLM/advanced/kv-cache-reuse.html", overlap: "Medium: shipping KV cache page reuse for same-prefix requests, LRU eviction, and system-prompt reuse; docs note large batches may launch same-prefix requests before reuse is available."}, {system: "TensorRT-LLM KV cache priority/event APIs", url: "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/introducing-new-kv-cache-reuse-optimizations-in-nvidia-tensorrt-llm/", overlap: "Medium: priority-based KV eviction and KV cache event API support KV-aware routing/scheduling decisions across executors; not the same bounded reorder-window admission."}, {system: "llm-d precise prefix-cache aware scheduling", url: "https://llm-d.ai/blog/kvcache-wins-you-can-see", overlap: "High at distributed-routing layer: balances load and prefix-cache affinity, claims precise prefix-cache-aware scheduling with vLLM cache introspection; not clearly same intra-engine batch admission/fairness cap."}]
CONTRIBUTION_TYPE: mechanism
SCALE_REALISM: L0 is insufficient for realistic systems claims. The conditional effect holds in a CPU discrete-event simulator only under eviction pressure plus queue depth, with constant service time and recomputed-prefix-token proxy. It has no real vLLM/SGLang/TensorRT-LLM scheduler, no paged-attention allocator behavior, no chunked prefill interaction, no wall-clock TTFT/throughput, and no bursty agentic-loop p99 validation. Required GPU pass: implement bounded-W fairness-aware admission inside or alongside SGLang/vLLM APC, compare against their native cache-aware schedulers, and report p50/p99 TTFT, throughput, KV hit rate, eviction, and fairness under realistic bursty multi-family traffic.
RATIONALE: PROMPT_VERSION=v001. The core cache-aware admission idea is already implemented/published in SGLang: RadixAttention uses LRU prefix KV reuse and “cache-aware scheduling” that sorts waiting requests by matched prefix length rather than FCFS for continuous batching (https://arxiv.org/html/2312.07104v1). vLLM and TensorRT-LLM also ship automatic prefix/KV cache reuse with LRU-style eviction, so prefix-family cache reuse itself is not an insight. The remaining possible contribution is the bounded reorder-window / matched-p99 fairness mechanism and measurement separating greedy cache affinity from fair cache affinity. The packet’s evidence supports that only conditionally: 15/92 matched cells have CI<0 wins, all concentrated in cache-too-small + heavy-load regimes; all-cache regimes are 0/32 wins; strongest cells show 67.8-76.4% recomputed-prefix-token savings at p99 <=1.10x FCFS, while unbounded greedy gives ~17% mean savings at 1.29-1.34x p99 wait. That is enough for yellow as a fairness-control mechanism, not green as a systems contribution, until reconciled against SGLang’s existing scheduler and reproduced on real serving stacks.
